# Day 76 – Full Observability Stack Review

## Metrics Pipeline

Metrics are collected from:

* Node Exporter (host metrics)
* cAdvisor (container metrics)
* OpenTelemetry Collector (OTLP metrics)

Prometheus scrapes these targets every 15 seconds and stores the data. Grafana queries Prometheus to create dashboards and alert rules.

Flow:

Node Exporter → Prometheus → Grafana

cAdvisor → Prometheus → Grafana

OTEL Collector → Prometheus → Grafana

Prometheus Alerts → Notifications

## Logs Pipeline

Docker containers generate logs.

Promtail collects log files from Docker containers and forwards them to Loki.

Grafana queries Loki to visualize and search logs.

Flow:

Docker Containers → Promtail → Loki → Grafana

## Traces Pipeline

OpenTelemetry Collector receives telemetry using OTLP over gRPC (4317) and HTTP (4318).

Traces are currently exported to the debug exporter for testing.

Flow:

Application / curl → OTEL Collector → Debug Exporter

Future:

Application → OTEL Collector → Tempo or Jaeger → Grafana

## Services

Prometheus (9090) – Metrics storage and querying

Node Exporter (9100) – Host metrics

cAdvisor (8080) – Container metrics

Grafana (3000) – Dashboards and alerting

Loki (3100) – Log storage

Promtail (9080) – Log collection

OTEL Collector (4317/4318/8889) – Telemetry collection

JioHotstar Application (8081) – Sample application

PostgreSQL (5432) – Application database

## Outcome

The observability stack now supports all three observability pillars:

1. Metrics
2. Logs
3. Traces

This enables monitoring, troubleshooting, alerting, and root cause analysis from a single Grafana interface.
